    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d715">

                <pb facs="0765" n="753" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg753"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/11857a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-06-09T21:00:00-04:00">June 9, 1941—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>776. According to reports received this weekend, principally from missions in
                    Bucharest and Stockholm,<anchor n="62" xml:id="d715-f1"/> Germany, while
                    pressing the Soviet Union actively for economic and political concessions, is
                    making immediate preparations for an invasion of the Soviet Union to take place
                    within the next fortnight. A Bucharest source, for instance, states that Germany
                    has delivered an ultimatum to the Soviet Union, to expire June 10, containing
                    the following demands: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Restitution to Finland of seized Finnish territories;</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>The evacuation of Soviet-occupied Poland;</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item>The return of the Baltic States to Germany;</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>The return of Bessarabia and Bukovina to Rumania;</item>
                        <label>5.</label>
                        <item>The lease of the Ukraine to Germany for thirty years;</item>
                        <label>6.</label>
                        <item>The transformation of the Soviet Union into a National Socialist state
                            with German control over the Army;</item>
                        <label>7.</label>
                        <item>The granting of an outlet on the Pacific to Germany.</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <p>Other sources report large concentrations of German troops in Tiflis and despatch
                    of German oil technicians to Baku.</p>
                <p>The reporting offices and the Department are inclined to treat these reports with
                    some reserve. Nevertheless, since they are coming almost simultaneously from
                    various points, it has been considered advisable to bring them to your attention
                    for such comment as you may care to make.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
